From: tebako-crypto feedstock
Subject: rnp 0.18.x: include <cstring> in crypto/mem.cpp (gcc 13)

mem.cpp uses strlen() without including <cstring>. It compiles on
macOS only because clang's libc++ leaks the declaration transitively;
gcc 13/libstdc++ (ubuntu-24.04) does not:

    error: 'strlen' was not declared in this scope

One-line include addition, identical to the fix upstream rnp main
carries in the same file.
--- a/src/lib/crypto/mem.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/crypto/mem.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstring>
 #include "mem.h"
 #include "logging.h"
 #include <botan/ffi.h>
